Mysterious Adventures
Mysterious Adventures is a 2D top-down adventure game currently in development using Unity and C#.
The game is set in a small world that the player can freely explore. The project focuses on creating an immersive environment with NPC interactions, exploration, and different gameplay systems.
Current Features

Player Movement
• 2D top-down player movement.
• 8-directional movement.
• Character facing direction based on the last movement direction.
• Camera follows the player.

World and Environment
• Tilemap-based world.
• Custom-designed environment and terrain.
• Connected road system using Unity Rule Tiles.
• Different areas are being created, including a village, forest, and farm.
• Custom pixel-art textures and sprites.

NPC System
• NPC characters with independent movement.
• Random wandering within defined areas.
• NPC interaction system.
• Interaction prompts when facing an NPC.

Dialogue System
• NPCs have predefined dialogue.
• Dialogue UI.
• Typewriter-style text animation.
• Dialogue can be skipped while text is being displayed.

Quest System
• Basic quest management system.
• Quest states, including not started, active, and completed.
• Quest objectives with target IDs and required amounts.

Inventory System
• Inventory with item slots.
• Item stacking.
• Hotbar with 9 selectable slots.
• Hotbar selection using number keys and the mouse scroll wheel.
• Ability to drop items.

Day and Night System
• Day and night cycle.
• Daytime tracking.
• UI displaying the current time of day.

Development Information
• Game Engine: Unity 6.2
• Programming Language: C#
• Render Pipeline: Universal Render Pipeline (URP)
• Perspective: 2D Top-Down
• Art Style: Pixel Art
The game is still actively being developed. New mechanics, content, and improvements are being added as development progresses.

AI Disclosure
AI tools were used as supplementary assistance during development, for, debugging.
The development, implementation, integration, and testing of the game's systems are carried out by the development team. AI is used as an assisting tool, not as a replacement for the team's work.
